{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Behold, strong.</b> A descriptor for the day or for the force." "<b>Sho'er qetev.</b> The first kaf is drawing after it [i.e., construct-linked], and so it is like 'kesho'er' (like one sweeping)." "<b>Qetev.</b> Like 'I will be your qetev, O Sheol' (Hosea 13:14)." "<b>He cast to the ground [by hand].</b> The meaning: that HaShem brought down these torrents, and cast them to the ground by His strong hand."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {3 "Bracketed [ביד] appears in the Hebrew lemma; included literally as [by hand] though the syntax is compressed and the referent of 'by hand' is resolved in the gloss as God's hand."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:30.802982661Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}